{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5524b81e-9fd7-4891-8c29-weapon-detection",
    "name": "Weapon Detection Backend API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Weapon Detection backend (ASP.NET Core). Covers every controller: Health, Auth, Branches, Devices, Device Activation, Detection Sync, Alerts, Dashboard, and Live Monitoring.\n\n## How to use\n\n1. Import the matching `Weapon Detection Local` environment and select it.\n2. Make sure the backend is running (`deployment/start.ps1`, default `http://localhost:8080`).\n3. Run folders **top to bottom** — later requests reuse values (`branchId`, `activationKey`, `deviceId`, `eventId`, `alertId`, ...) saved automatically by earlier ones via each request's Tests script.\n4. Easiest: select the collection and click **Run** (Collection Runner) to execute the whole flow end to end. The `Cleanup` folder at the bottom deletes the test branch and logs out.\n\n## Two kinds of authentication\n\n- **Admin JWT** (`Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`) — used by every Branches/Devices/Alerts/Dashboard/Live Monitoring endpoint. Obtained from `Auth > POST Login`. This is the collection's default auth.\n- **Device credentials** (`X-Device-Id` + `X-Device-Secret` headers) — used by the endpoints a Jetson Agent calls: Activate, Validate Device Credentials, Get Device Configuration, Sync Events, Upload Alert Snapshot. These requests set `auth: noauth` and add the headers explicitly, using `{{deviceId}}` / `{{sharedSecret}}` saved after Activation.\n\nEvery response is wrapped in the standard envelope: `{ \"success\": bool, \"message\": string|null, \"data\": object|null, \"errorCode\": string|null }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          ""
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          ""
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
